"<strong>Expansion.</strong> L = L₀[{#} + α(T − {#} °C)] with the textbook's average α. The flask level is h = (ΔV_liquid − ΔV_flask)/A with β_Pyrex = {#} × {#}⁻⁶ /°C. Water uses Tanaka et al. (Metrologia {#}, {#}, {#}) for its density, so it reproduces the minimum volume at {#} °C.",
"<strong>Conduction.</strong> Steady state only: P = AΔT/ΣR with R = d/k for each layer and the ASHRAE air film resistances ({#} m²·°C/W for still indoor air, {#} in a {#} km/h wind, {#} in a {#} km/h wind). A still air layer added to <strong>Window</strong> is conduction only; a real gap also carries heat by convection and radiation, so real double glazing passes about twice what the demo shows.",
"Homework: why do engineers quote R values (resistance per area) rather than conductivities? Convert the house wall's ΣR = {#} m²·°C/W into the US R value (ft²·°F·h/BTU, multiply by {#}).",
